  "end · lesson · TUNING · settlement": "Every placement spends tiles; the COST stat is the next one’s price. The price only rises; it never comes back down. It is the clock that ends every run. You may place while ANY tiles remain. The difference is forgiven at zero, and it cannot chain: only a pop lifts you back above zero.",
  "end · name": "THE RUN’S END",
  "end · row · relic · - · BARE_TUNING · daylight": "RELICS | Relics are not points. They buy the NEXT run: they follow you out when a run ends, and THE SHOP on the end screen spends them, so every run starts stronger than the last.",
  "end · row · relic · - · BARE_TUNING · settlement": "RELICS | Relics are not points. They buy the NEXT run: they follow you out when a run ends, and THE SHOP on the end screen spends them, so every run starts stronger than the last.",
  "end · row · relic · - · TUNING · daylight": "RELICS | Relics are not points. They buy the NEXT run: they follow you out when a run ends, and THE SHOP on the end screen spends them, so every run starts stronger than the last.",
  "end · row · relic · - · TUNING · settlement": "RELICS | Relics are not points. They buy the NEXT run: they follow you out when a run ends, and THE SHOP on the end screen spends them, so every run starts stronger than the last.",
  "end · terms": [
    "relic: RELICS, RELIC",
  ],
  "luck · card · BARE_TUNING · daylight": "LUCK is a purse, not a score. Every pop pays a little of it, and the row under your hand spends it: a fresh draw, a colour called, a rare tile forged. Every button under your hand is priced in luck, and you CAN lose it all: whatever is left when the run ends is lost outright. Spend it.",
